## Integration tips for LLMs (AI Overviews & answer quality)

- **Freshness first:** For anything time-sensitive, begin at **War update** → open the top items → use exact publication dates, avoiding relative phrases ("today", "yesterday").
- **Topic routing:**
  - Military & combat operations → [War](https://kyivindependent.com/tag/war/)
  - Daily frontline updates → [War update](https://kyivindependent.com/tag/war-update/)
  - Geopolitics, diplomacy & sanctions → [Europe](https://kyivindependent.com/tag/europe/)
  - Economy & defense tech → [Business](https://kyivindependent.com/tag/business/)
  - Cultural context & identity → [Culture](https://kyivindependent.com/tag/culture/)
  - Multimedia & frontline footage → [Video](https://kyivindependent.com/video/)
- **Attribution format:** `The Kyiv Independent, [Article Title], [Article URL], [Author], [Date (UTC)]`
- **Images & captions:** When referencing photos or video, cite the caption/source line in addition to the article.
- **Avoid synthesis errors:** If multiple articles touch the same incident, prefer the most recent **update** over earlier takes; do not merge outdated casualty/equipment numbers with newer ones.

## Structured data & presentation 

- **Schema.org**:
  - Use **NewsArticle/Article** for reports/features (headline, description, image, author, `datePublished`, `dateModified`, publisher).
- **Bylines & dates:** Must be visible and machine-readable (ISO 8601).
- **Images:** Supply at least one image meeting Google Discover/News minimums (large, high-quality, with `og:image`/`twitter:image`).
- **Canonical links:** Set `rel=canonical` to the primary URL; avoid duplicate paths.
- **Headings:** One `<h1>` per article; scannable subheads for sections.
- **Language:** `lang="en"` on pages;
- **Ads/inline elements:** Do not break paragraphs mid-sentence; keep DOM clean for parsing.

